AcquisitionMethod: nanoLC–MS/MS
AcquisitionMethod: data-dependent MS/MS
AlkylationReagent: chloroacetamide
Bait: poly(A)–RNA
CellLine: K562 (ATTC)
CellPart: nuclei
CellPart: chromatin
CleavageAgent: trypsin
CollisionEnergy: normalised collision energy of 25 eV
DevelopmentalStage: proliferating
EnrichmentMethod: serial RNA interactome capture
EnrichmentMethod: serIC
EnrichmentMethod: oligo(dT) dynabeads
FactorValue: crosslinked
FactorValue: non-crosslinked control
FlowRateChromatogram: 266 nl min −1
FractionIdentifier: pH levels 11, 8, 6, 5, 4 and 3
FractionationMethod: strong anion-exchange chromatography
FractionationMethod: SCX
GradientTime: 180 min
Instrument: Thermo Scientific Q-Exactive Plus Orbitrap mass spectrometer
IonizationType: Nanoelectrospray
Label: label-free quantification
Label: LFQ
MaterialType: cells
MaterialType: cell line
Modification: Cysteine carbamidomethylation
Modification: N-terminal acetylation
Modification: methionine oxidation
NumberOfBiologicalReplicates: 2
NumberOfFractions: six pH fractions
NumberOfFractions: five strong anion-exchange chromatography fractions
NumberOfMissedCleavages: two
Organism: human
OrganismPart: nuclei
PooledSample: pooled
ReductionReagent: DTT
Separation: nanoflow reverse-phase liquid chromatography (Dionex Ultimate 3000, Thermo Scientific)
Separation: PicoFrit analytical column (75 μm ID × 25 cm long, 15 μm Tip ID (New Objectives, Woburn, MA) packed in-house with 3 μm C18 resin (Reprosil-AQ Pur, Dr Maisch, Ammerbuch-Entringen, Germany)
Staining: silver staining
Temperature: 37 °C
Treatment: irradiated in a stratalinker with 0.4 J cm−2 UVC light (256 nm)
Treatment: non-crosslinked control
